TRANSVERSE IN THE SOLVE WORKS.  It pays down the relocated debt on every
airport (CYXY 188->51, below the battery's own 63; SPJC 331->167; HECA
572->155) and it binds essentially everything the census prices: CYXY
bound 3066/3067, SPJC 8477/8491, HECA 26616/26629.  STEPS recede from the
apronpop arm but do NOT return to battery (SPJC 37->31, HECA 192->131).

THE STOP — SPJC, and it is an INTERACTION, not either change.  A 2x2 was
measured (one extra arm, O4_APRON_WITHIN_SHAPE_FRONTAGE_ONLY=0, 236 s):

  | SPJC arm                     | airside | within_shape | transverse | steps |
  |------------------------------|---------|--------------|------------|-------|
  | battery (neither)            |   189   |      45      |     46     |   0   |
  | apronpop only                |   474   |      12      |    331     |  37   |
  | transect only (flag-off arm) |   195   |      62      |     32     |   0   |
  | COMPOSED                     |   551   |     258      |    167     |  31   |

Neither change alone mints the within_shape blow-up (12 and 62); composed is
258.  231 of the NEW rows are within_shape apron|apron AIRSIDE, and the
population is CORRECT — 201 of the 233 apron rows are frontage chords, so this
is not a predicate defect.  MECHANISM: apronpop withdraws the generic apron
pair law, leaving the building->spine frontage chord as the ONLY apron
within-shape law; the transverse hyper rows then move the apron surface by
metres (airside_value_delta 3797 nodes moved, worst 9.66 m) and the frontage
chords absorb the whole displacement.  The carrier regularisation (spec §5,
"do not add a replacement regulariser") does not hold the apron interior
against an ACTIVE cross-corridor projection — it only smooths a seed.

