BUILD HYGIENE.  Six harness builds, all rc=0, all "shared repo UNCHANGED by
this build (full-surface before/after snapshot)".  No --no-ledger, no
--allow-degraded-dem, no timing claim.  The three log-capture reruns exist
only because the first three builds were piped through `tail` and lost the
solve-side instrument lines; they are byte-identical arms, not new arms.

WHAT IS OWED
  1. THE SPJC STOP.  The frontage chord cannot be the apron's only
     within-shape law while an active transverse projection moves the
     surface under it.  This is an owner/spec question, not an
     implementation one: either the ruled population needs a corridor-
     interior term, or the transverse rows need to price the frontage
     chord's own direction.  Do not improvise a regulariser (spec §5
     forbids exactly that).
  2. broken_by_emit at 54-65 % — the "nothing moves after the final
     projection" spec A1 §8d exists to trigger.
  3. SPLP / KAFW / KDFW have no arm under this tree (three of the six
     battery airports).
  4. HECA's 91 frontage rows > 5 % and the CYXY 37 % spine row remain
     unfixed and un-adjudicated.
